		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Voila un bon exercice pour se débloquer le cerveau en ce début de semaine !<br />Une première idée....<br />Cdlt</p><br /><p>select * from debit;<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; date&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;| debit<br />---------------------+-------<br /> 2012-01-01 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;1.2<br /> 2012-01-02 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;8.4<br /> 2012-01-03 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;8.2<br /> 2012-01-04 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;1.0<br /> 2012-01-05 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;1.0<br /> 2012-01-06 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;1.0<br /> 2012-01-07 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;1.0<br /> 2012-01-08 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;1.4<br /> 2012-01-09 00:00:00 |&#160; 51.4<br /> 2012-01-10 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;0.4<br /> 2012-01-11 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;0.4<br /> 2012-01-12 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;0.4<br /> 2012-01-13 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;0.0<br /> 2012-01-14 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;0.0<br />(14 lignes)</p><br /><p>select min(D1) date_debut, debit, count(*)+1 from<br />(select d1.date D1, d2.date D2, d1.debit Debit&#160; from debit d1, debit d2<br />where d2.date = d1.date + interval &#039;1 day&#039; ::interval and d1.debit=d2.debit and d1.debit &gt;= 0) R1<br />group by debit;<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;date_debut| debit | ?column?<br />---------------------+-------+----------<br /> 2012-01-13 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;0.0 |&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2<br /> 2012-01-10 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;0.4 |&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 3<br /> 2012-01-04 00:00:00 |&#160; &#160;1.0 |&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 4</p>]]></content>
